<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Commercial Union lifts headline yr shr,div.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union lifts headline yr shr,div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>	     -- headline	252.2    vs    251.8</p>
<p>	     -- ordinary	353.2    vs    251.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    90.0    vs     75.0</p>
<p>    Net income		  176.6    vs    125.9</p>
<p>    Net premium income    1,520.4    vs  1,204.7</p>
<p>    Gross premium income  1,901.6    vs  1,525.2</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit	33.3    vs     38.1</p>
<p>    Investment income	 118.7    vs     73.7</p>
<p>Div payable April 9</p>
<p>On register March 14</p>
<p>Full name: Commercial Union of South Africa Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said its acquisition last November of the entire share capital of Protea Life Company Limited and Protea Assurance Investment Management Limited would enable it to strengthen its presence in the competitive life assurance market. It said the acquisition provided it with a base to provide significant growth in the provision of investment products.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
